# .release-removals — paths this repository used to publish and deliberately no longer does.
#
# If a file you could once fetch from here has gone, the reason belongs in this file: what moved,
# and where to look for it now. A removal is not forbidden; an unexplained one is, because from
# outside there is no way to tell a deliberate withdrawal from a mistake.
#
# One path or path-prefix per line. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.

# ⭐ NOTHING IS LISTED, AND THAT IS A MEASUREMENT RATHER THAN AN OVERSIGHT.
# No version of this repository has been published yet, so there is no earlier public tree for
# anything to have disappeared from. The first release adds files and withdraws none.
#
# Two things worth knowing if you are the next person here: a path that stops being published is
# just as invisible to a reader as a path that is deleted, so both belong above; and if you
# de-version a filename — `…-v1.<ext>` to `…-<ext>` — assume something out there pins the old one.
